  "2026-07-25T04:47:03.333Z",claude-code-agent,"Release-health completion 2026-07-25: PR #698 merged as 84694f6e after a complete exact-head review inventory with zero unresolved or unreacted bot surfaces. Production Auto Release run 30144035888 succeeded in 17m34s and waited for publication; the single daily tag v2026.7.25 points to release commit e893e5ad, GitHub Release is live, and npm latest is @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.7.25. Authenticated Sentry/telemetry gate passes with critical=0, high=0, finish_error_rate_pct=2.03, and zero failures missing error codes. pm health reports telemetry endpoint 200, last successful real-time flush at 2026-07-25T04:44:49.632Z, queue draining normally, history drift zero, and no actionable unknown-author events. Isolated anonymous-registry installed-package proof in a temporary directory passed version, init, create, comments, get, health, and validate without PM_AUTHOR; both mutations were attributed automatically to harness:codex. Returning this recurring reminder to open and unclaimed."
  "2026-07-26T12:59:17.893Z","harness:codex","Investigation 2026-07-26: broad SDK release gates passed build, static quality, literal 100/100/100/100 coverage, packed npx smoke, and 88-command package dogfood, then failed only because an environment Sentry token returned 403. The installed Sentry CLI is authenticated and successfully reads unbrained/pm-cli, exposing a gate defect: best-effort mode falls back to CLI credentials only when no token exists, not when every environment token is rejected. Reusing this canonical all-status release-health reminder; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-07-26T13:11:40.068Z","harness:codex","Fix evidence 2026-07-26: best-effort release telemetry now falls back to the authenticated Sentry CLI after all configured API tokens fail, while telemetry-off mode retains direct API diagnostics and tokenless best-effort remains optional. Focused 51-test regression suite passed. Adversarial live run with only an intentionally invalid SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN passed via token_source=sentry_cli: critical=0, high=0, four expected handled groups, telemetry finish_error_rate_pct=1.98, and zero failures missing error_code. Full local product gates passed 6,420 tests at literal 100/100/100/100 plus packed npx and 88-command dogfood; only pre-push exact-SHA hosted analysis remains pending."
  "2026-07-26T13:18:31.719Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: broad delivery published as GitHub PR #744 (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/744) from branch feat/sdk-agent-fleet-integrity. Exact implementation commit c13e4aca; hosted checks and full AI review loop pending on the PR head."
  "2026-07-26T14:09:10.793Z","harness:codex","Exact-head hosted evidence: PR #744 commit b28d3cb736a32cbcd54266243cd3f6848372f6df passed the complete required GitHub check matrix with zero failed checks. Thread-aware inventory found zero inline threads. CodeRabbit completed the explicitly retriggered full-review request under its external fair-usage limit and emitted no finding; all new bot surfaces were reacted to and acknowledged. Local final evidence remains 374 files, 6,420 tests, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, clean lint/static/contracts/changelog/health, and real-time telemetry drain."
  "2026-07-26T14:27:08.367Z","harness:codex","GitHub report linkage: GH-746 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/746. Release run 30183263363 published v2026.7.26 with --access public and provenance, but hermetic anonymous npm metadata and tarball requests now return 404 while authenticated/cached lookup can appear healthy. Reusing the canonical recurring release-health item; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-07-26T14:47:00.530Z","harness:codex","Evidence: release publication now distinguishes fresh anonymous visibility from protected authenticated existence, can restore scoped-package public status without publishing a second immutable version, and verifies npm/npx/bunx with empty credentials plus isolated npm/Bun caches. Focused workflow/verifier tests, complete 6420-test 100% coverage, lint/static quality/contracts/docs links/audit passed. Live same-tag recovery remains intentionally deferred until this workflow change reaches protected main."
  "2026-07-26T15:08:42.936Z","harness:codex","Acceptance update: native pm test executed all 17 linked checks. Sixteen passed; the first aggregate release-gate attempt alone observed a transient CLI transport-floor slowdown after sustained concurrent/heavy validation (get 439ms>362ms, next 513ms>440ms, create 466ms>398ms, claim 495ms>415ms). The isolated transport floor immediately passed all six operations, and a fresh quiet aggregate release-gate rerun then passed end to end: static quality, 374 files/6420 tests at 100/100/100/100, secret scan, packed npx smoke, 88-command package dogfood, version policy, and release gates. The failed measurement remains recorded rather than being misreported as green."
  "2026-07-26T15:12:40.688Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/748. Initial exact implementation commit 004790f7; protected-main same-tag npm visibility recovery remains pending merge and will not publish a second v2026.7.26 artifact."
  "2026-07-26T15:17:54.559Z","harness:codex","CI review response for PR #748: Windows regression exposed a platform-specific test expectation introduced by this work; production code behaved correctly, but the spec hard-coded POSIX paths while path.join emits Windows separators. Replaced those expectations with top-level node:path joins. Focused 23-test verifier suite and ESLint pass locally; Windows hosted rerun pending on the new exact head."
  "2026-07-26T15:24:35.741Z","harness:codex","Exact-head pre-merge evidence for PR #748: commit eeb768ba50dde4c902ced790798e93ff43eb0f71 has zero failed or pending GitHub checks after the single transient GitHub artifact-download retry. The public-registry verifier, same-tag access recovery, full 6,420-test 100/100/100/100 local coverage, strict quality/security gates, isolated packed consumer, and npm/npx/bunx credential-isolation contracts are green. CodeRabbit and Sourcery quota notices and unavailable Greptile review are reviewer-infrastructure limits, not product findings. Production v2026.7.26 anonymous visibility recovery remains the next post-merge action; this recurring reminder returns to open while awaiting that live proof."
  "2026-07-26T15:40:57.788Z","harness:codex","Production failure evidence 2026-07-26: merged PR #748 recovery run 30208359946 passed every build, coverage, static, compatibility, reliability, packaging, npx, and dogfood gate, then failed in Publish to npm. Both fresh anonymous and token-authenticated npm view returned 404 for hidden @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.26, so the branch attempted npm publish; npm then proved the immutable version exists by rejecting overwrite. Root cause: authenticated metadata lookup is not a reliable existence oracle for this hidden package state. Required recovery is access-first: after anonymous miss, attempt npm access set status=public; publish only when access reports the package does not exist."
  "2026-07-26T15:52:21.915Z","harness:codex","Fix evidence: release publication now treats fresh anonymous visibility as the only skip condition. After an anonymous miss it attempts npm access set status=public before any immutable publish; only a definitive npm E404/package-not-found response permits publication, while authentication, permission, and registry failures stop fail-closed. The authenticated npm view oracle that failed in run 30208359946 is removed. Focused workflow contracts pass 27/27, ESLint and docs links pass, npm 11.17.0 help confirms the access syntax, strict repository lint passes with zero duplication, 100% docstring quality, package boundaries, token budgets, SDK surface/import costs, and transport floor; contracts and high-severity audit are clean."
  "2026-07-26T15:53:14.123Z","harness:codex","Recovery follow-up PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/750 at initial implementation commit c5280477. Exact-head hosted checks, AI review inventory, merge, and production rerun remain pending."
  "2026-07-26T15:58:28.309Z","harness:codex","Exact-head hosted evidence for PR #750: cc0c058a1c3bbc7547b7ccdf3a3f20362bd4ab09 passes 31 checks with zero failed or pending, including ShellCheck/actionlint, Trivy/TruffleHog/Semgrep/CodeQL, full coverage aggregation, static/typecheck/compat/smokes, Windows/macOS/Node runtimes, docs, DeepScan zero findings, CodeFactor, unchanged-performance CodSpeed, and Codecov complete modified-line coverage. Thread inventory is empty. External reviewer quotas produced no actionable finding. Returning this recurring reminder to open/unclaimed while the exact merged-main production rerun remains the next action."
  "2026-07-26T16:20:49.965Z","harness:codex","Production blocker evidence 2026-07-26: merged PR #750 recovery run 30209544683 passed build, static, compatibility, reliability/Sentry, source maps, package smoke, npx, and 88-command dogfood. The initial coverage leg observed one nondeterministic V8 instrumentation miss at 99.99% lines/statements; rerunning only that unchanged failed job restored literal 100/100/100/100 without lowering any threshold. Publish then executed the new access-first path and  failed E403. The workflow stopped fail-closed and did not attempt an immutable republish. Fresh anonymous metadata remains 404, while package access is private. GitHub issue #746 is reopened with maintainer action: use an npm account/token authorized to change package visibility, replace or upgrade the GitHub release environment NPM_TOKEN, set @unbraind/pm-cli public, then rerun the existing v2026.7.26 release workflow. This is an external npm authorization blocker, not a product-gate or duplicate-release failure."
  "2026-07-26T16:21:08.651Z","harness:codex","Correction to the immediately preceding evidence comment: the Publish step command was npm access set status=public @unbraind/pm-cli. It returned E403 in GitHub Actions run 30209544683. No immutable republish was attempted."
  "2026-07-26T17:10:01.200Z","harness:claude-code","Release health verified live 2026-07-26. npm dist-tag latest is 2026.7.26 and the tarball resolves; git tag v2026.7.26 and the matching GitHub release both exist; npx and bunx both execute the published artifact. The scheduled Auto Release run for today (30189918337) completed in 47 seconds with skipped true and 'No new pushed release tag detected', which is the same-day guard behaving correctly after the 01:39Z cut rather than a failure. The issues-closed trigger on the workflow is fenced by an if condition to the blocker-recovery path only, and every recent issues-triggered run shows as skipped, so closing an issue cannot cut a second release. Two auto-releases in one day therefore remain structurally impossible without an explicit dispatch."
  "2026-07-26T18:30:16.045Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health verification 2026-07-26 (live, not from memory or summary).\n\nRegistry and distribution:\n- npm view @unbrained/pm-cli version -> 2026.7.26\n- dist-tags -> latest: 2026.7.26 (single tag, no prerelease pointer)\n- HEAD on dist.tarball -> HTTP/2 200\n- npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@latest --version -> 2026.7.26\n- bunx @unbrained/pm-cli@latest --version -> 2026.7.26 (resolved, downloaded, extracted, lockfile written)\n\nBoth npm and bun runners install and execute the published package, so the\nGH-746 unavailability (metadata and tarball 404) and the GH-681 latest-points-\nat-prerelease condition are both clear on the live registry as of this check.\n\nRelease cadence:\n- gh release list -> v2026.7.26 (2026-07-26T01:46:57Z) is Latest, preceded by\n  v2026.7.25, v2026.7.24-3, v2026.7.23, v2026.7.22 — one dated release per day,\n  no duplicate same-day AUTO cut.\n- The same-day guard is structural rather than advisory: scripts/release/\n  run-release-pipeline.mjs:384 rejects the removed --allow-same-day-release flag\n  outright and directs a partial failure to retry the existing tag through the\n  Release workflow instead of cutting a replacement version.\n- The auto-release workflow's non-schedule entry points are fenced: the\n  issues:closed trigger only proceeds for a github-actions[bot]-authored issue\n  titled exactly \"Auto Release blocked: scheduled run failed\", and that recovery\n  path re-runs the exact failed tag workflow rather than creating a new version.\n- concurrency group auto-release-${{ github.workflow }} with\n  cancel-in-progress: false serializes overlapping runs.\n\nRepository signal sweep on the same date:\n- Open PRs: 0.\n- Open issues: 32, and every one of them carries at least one pm-item link\n  comment (verified by enumerating comment bodies per issue).\n- Dependabot alerts: 0 open.\n- Secret-scanning alerts: 1, state resolved, resolution false_positive.\n- Code-scanning alerts: 2 open, both OpenSSF Scorecard meta-findings rather than\n  code defects — CII-Best-Practices (low) and Code-Review (high). The\n  Code-Review finding reflects the maintainer's deliberate direct-to-main\n  workflow, so it is an accepted posture, not a defect to remediate."
  "2026-07-26T22:35:17.245Z","harness:opencode","2026-07-26 verification (session pm-v4iypw): pipeline healthy and same-day idempotence structurally enforced. Live checks: npm latest=2026.7.26, tag v2026.7.26 released 2026-07-26T01:46Z. Code checks: run-release-pipeline.mjs maybeSkipForSameDayRelease() skips when any same-day tag exists; skips on no_changes_since_last_tag and on tracker-only changes; --allow-same-day-release removed (retry goes through the Release workflow on the existing tag). auto-release.yml issues-path guards: same-UTC-day window, one retry per blocker issue per day (auto-release-retry-attempted marker), existing same-day tag triggers rerun of its Release workflow instead of a new version. Executor verification post-publish (verify-published-release.mjs): npm metadata, npx direct, npx --package, bunx --bun. Known gap remains tracked: pm-lpqln4 (bunx gate token-position weakness), pm-2z9263 (publish-scope guard dead code). No new item filed."
  "2026-07-28T02:58:50.750Z","harness:claude-code","Release health 2026-07-28. Recording because the path changed, not to restate a healthy day.\n\nState: npm latest is 2026.7.28 and dist-tags carry only latest. The published artifact runs under BOTH runtimes - npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@latest --version prints 2026.7.28, and bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@latest --version prints 2026.7.28 after writing a lockfile. A real workflow against the published package succeeded end to end under npx: init exited 0, create wrote an item, and list returned count 1.\n\nWhat changed: today's release was NOT cut by the scheduled run. Auto Release 30318124311 (workflow_dispatch) FAILED at 00:42Z on the sentry-telemetry-gate with telemetry_query_command_missing, and 30318608865 (workflow_dispatch, 18m54s) succeeded at 00:52Z and cut 2026.7.28. CI for the resulting cut commit passed in 3m24s. The last schedule-triggered run was 2026-07-27T06:05:09Z; today's scheduled run had not fired at the time of this check.\n\nConsequence for the one-per-day guarantee, verified rather than assumed: the tag v2026.7.28 already exists, so when today's scheduled run fires it will match the same-day guard and skip. That is the correct outcome and no second auto-release will occur today. Two separate defects were filed from checking this rather than trusting it - the telemetry gate mode being unsatisfiable in hosted CI is recorded on the local-versus-hosted parity item, and the same-day guard's prefix-glob comparison being correct only by accident of tag ordering is now its own issue.\n\nTrigger-path reliability over the last 100 auto-release runs, worth separating because the two paths behave very differently: workflow_dispatch is 12 runs with 5 successes and 7 failures, while schedule is 4 runs with 3 successes and 1 failure. The issues trigger accounts for 84 runs of which 76 skipped and 7 cancelled, consistent with the blocker-recovery fence rather than real release work.\n"
  "2026-07-28T15:00:23.380Z","harness:claude-code","Release health verified live 2026-07-28. npm latest is 2026.7.28, git tag v2026.7.28 exists, and both published entry points run the real artifact: npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@latest pm --version and bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@latest pm --version each print 2026.7.28 and exit 0.\n\nThe one-per-day guarantee held under the case that looks like a violation. Two Auto Release runs completed successfully today: workflow_dispatch 30330976595 at 05:12:56Z and schedule 30331935213 at 05:32:33Z. Only one version was cut. The scheduled run's log records reason release_already_cut_today and the pipeline logs the branch that retries the existing tag's Release workflow rather than creating another version — Same-day tag already exists; retrying its exact Release workflow instead of creating another version. A successful Auto Release run is therefore not evidence that a release was cut, and a second same-day success is the guard working, not failing.\n\nAlso live: two Auto Release runs at 14:21Z were triggered by the issues event from the nightly blocker issues for windows-latest Node 24 and macos-latest Node 24, and both correctly skipped. That trigger stays fenced to blocker recovery."
  "2026-07-28T22:38:57.572Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health verification 2026-07-28 (UTC). Reported because the run counts changed, not to restate a healthy day.\n\nPublished state: npm latest is 2026.7.28, the only dist-tag is latest, and git tag v2026.7.28 exists. Exactly one release reached npm for the UTC day.\n\nAuto Release ran 25 times on 2026-07-28. Four of those completed successfully - 00:52 workflow_dispatch, 05:12 workflow_dispatch, 05:32 schedule, 19:08 workflow_dispatch - and one failed at 00:42 (run 30318124311, the known unsatisfiable --telemetry-mode required leg in hosted CI, owned by pm-ei6x66). The remaining twenty were issues-triggered and skipped in one to ten seconds. Four successes and one published version is the guard working as designed: maybeSkipForSameDayRelease returns release_already_cut_today and the workflow still concludes success. A success count is therefore not a release count and must never be read as one.\n\nThe scheduled run fired at 05:32:33Z against a cron of 35 2 * * *, consistent with the drift pm-44u3wt owns and unchanged by anything this pass.\n\nBoth published-artifact runners were exercised end to end against 2026.7.28 rather than only for --version, in separate clean sandboxes:\n\n  npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@latest   -> version 2026.7.28, then init, then create returned pm-ckmg, then list-open returned that item\n  bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@latest -> version 2026.7.28, then init, then create returned pm-c4sm, then list-open returned that item, under bun 1.3.11\n\n[Unreleased] is non-empty at 22 entries, so the next scheduled cut has work to publish.\n"
  "2026-07-29T04:42:15.600Z","harness:claude-code","Release cadence verified live 2026-07-29. npm dist-tag latest is 2026.7.29 and the published version list ends 2026.7.23, 2026.7.24-3, 2026.7.24, 2026.7.25, 2026.7.26, 2026.7.27, 2026.7.28, 2026.7.29 - one calendar version per day for seven consecutive days, matching git tags v2026.7.25 through v2026.7.29 with no same-day duplicate. Today's cut came from a workflow_dispatch run at 02:09Z that succeeded in 18m23s; the scheduled run had not yet fired at the time of measurement, and when it does the same-day guard is the control that must skip it. Run-event mix over the last three days: 2026-07-27 seven runs, all issues-triggered, all skipped; 2026-07-28 twenty-five runs of which twenty were issues-triggered skips, one schedule, four workflow_dispatch, resolving to four successes, four cancellations and one failure but exactly one published version; 2026-07-29 eight runs, seven issues skips and the one dispatch success. The four cancellations on 2026-07-28 are the concurrency key collapsing an issues burst and are not release failures. Conclusion for this item: the one-auto-release-per-day invariant holds on the published artifact, and the evidence for it is the npm version list rather than the run count, because successful runs and published versions are not one to one."
  "2026-07-29T17:04:47.112Z","harness:claude-code","Release procedure verified live 2026-07-29.\n\nOne release per day holds, and the guard was observed firing rather than inferred. Release v2026.7.29 was cut at 02:27 UTC and is the npm latest version; the local package version matches at 2026.7.29. A second Auto Release run at 14:39 UTC, run id 30461972822, was a workflow_dispatch triggered by an issue closure and it completed with conclusion success in 45 seconds while publishing nothing - its log contains skipped true and reason release_already_cut_today, followed by \"No new pushed release tag detected; publish dispatch skipped\". Git tags and GitHub releases both show exactly one entry per day for 07-26 through 07-29 with no same-day duplicates and no prerelease suffixes.\n\nThe standing caution is worth restating because it recurred today: a successful Auto Release run is not a cut. Two successes on one day are the healthy outcome when the second is the guard declining.\n\nDistribution verified in the same session: npx and bunx both execute the published 2026.7.29 artifact through a real init, create and read sequence under bun 1.3.11 as well as node. A bunx cold-cache stdout hazard found while doing so is recorded on the acceptance item rather than here.\n"
  "2026-07-30T17:16:26.523Z","harness:claude-code","Release health verified 2026-07-30 (evening). One cut today and the one-per-day guarantee held under load.\n\nAuto Release runs today: one scheduled run at 05:24Z that succeeded and published, and four issues-triggered runs at 08:52Z, 09:54Z and twice at 14:33Z that all fenced to skipped. Four successes plus skips is still one release, which is the distinction this item exists to keep straight. npm latest is 2026.7.30 and the only dist-tag is latest, so no prerelease is sitting in front of the stable range. Tag v2026.7.30 exists in git.\n\nExecutor verification on the published artifact, not on a local build: npx at the exact version prints 2026.7.30, and bunx with the bun runtime prints 2026.7.30 under bun 1.3.11. The bunx run was warmed first, because a cold bun cache writes installer chatter to standard output ahead of command output and breaks any parser reading the first line.\n\nMain CI is green on every completed run today, six in a row including the merge commit for the context-budget bundle. The nightly matrix was red at 06:30Z on a commit that predates the Windows root-contract fix, and a run dispatched at HEAD after that fix and after the context-budget bundle is green across all legs, so the failure surface is closed at the current commit rather than merely quiet.\n\nNothing here changes this item's scope, which stays the per-day procedure. The same-day boundary riding a drifting start instant and the failure rate over the whole run history remain with their own owners."
  "2026-07-31T10:18:47.218Z","harness:codex","Release health verified live 2026-07-31. Scheduled Auto Release run 30607915788 completed successfully from 05:50Z to 06:11Z and produced the single public v2026.7.31 release. GitHub releases show one dated release for each day from v2026.7.25 through v2026.7.31, with exactly one v2026.7.31 entry. npm reports latest=2026.7.31 and no alternate dist-tag. In a fresh unrelated temporary directory, npm exec resolved pm inside its isolated _npx package root and printed 2026.7.31; bunx with Bun printed 2026.7.31. Current main CI runs are green. This proves today's artifact and both consumer paths, but does not erase the longitudinal reliability and schedule-drift defects pm-e70zh5 and pm-44u3wt or the guard-key defect pm-ki67py; the recurring reminder remains open."
  "2026-08-01T09:53:07.998Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health check performed 2026-08-01T09:30Z. npm dist-tags.latest is 2026.8.1, published 02:43:26Z; GitHub release v2026.8.1 created 02:44:13Z; git tag v2026.8.1 present. Today's daily cut published successfully and exactly once. Package-manager coverage of that artifact is exercised by scripts/release/verify-published-release.mjs, which the Release workflow runs after publish under both Node and Bun toolchains (oven-sh/setup-bun in .github/workflows/release.yml:190): it drives npx-pm and bunx-pm through a real CLI dispatch (contracts --summary), npx-pm-mcp and bunx-pm-mcp through JSON-RPC initialization, and asserts missing-bin control cases for both executors so a false pass on a nonexistent binary is detectable. This reminder has no re-arm mechanism and will not fire again on its own; pm-hipfu9 owns that."
  "2026-08-01T13:13:49.140Z","harness:claude-code","Release health 2026-08-01. One cut for the day and it is correct. npm latest is 2026.8.1, git tag v2026.8.1 exists, and the auto-release run history shows exactly one scheduled success at 05:41Z plus two workflow_dispatch successes earlier and two issues-triggered runs that both resolved to skipped. The one-per-day guard is behaving as designed and a successful run is still not the same thing as a cut.\n\nPublished-artifact behavior is split and the split is now filed. Working: npx --yes @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.1 init, and list-open after it, and the disambiguated forms npx --yes --package SPEC -- pm ... and bunx --silent --bun --package SPEC pm ..., which are the forms the release verifier uses. Failing: npx --yes @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.1 pm init and the bunx equivalent, both exit 2 with \"Unknown command pm\", and the same for the pm-cli token. Neither runner dispatches on the bin name in that position; both forward it as an argument. Tested against 2026.7.28 and 2026.7.31 as well, with identical results, so this is a long-standing property rather than a regression in today's cut. The reason no prior verification caught it is that the ad-hoc probes used pm --version, which short-circuits before dispatch and exits 0 on the broken form."
  "2026-08-02T15:05:35.523Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health check 2026-08-02: one cut today and only one. npm @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.2; git tag v2026.8.2 published 2026-08-02T00:21:22Z; package.json 2026.8.2 at HEAD 20cc2c9bf. All eight auto-release runs visible today fired on the 'issues: closed' trigger and every one resolved to 'skipped', which is the same-day fence behaving as designed - a successful run is not a cut. Published-artifact acceptance verified live against the published tarball, not the local build: 'npx --yes @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.2 --version' -> 2026.8.2 and 'bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.2 --version' -> 2026.8.2. No second auto-release occurred."
  "2026-08-03T02:18:59.082Z","harness:codex","2026-08-03 recovery evidence: Auto Release run 30775382287 exposed nondeterministic procfs coverage and was fixed in merged PR #875. Run 30777561730 passed code/package gates but intentionally failed because telemetry_mode=required has no hosted private query adapter, the already-recorded pm-ei6x66 limitation. Production-contract run 30778432132 used telemetry_mode=off and passed exact 100% coverage, version 2026.8.3 policy, secrets, npx packed smoke, 88-command dogfood, and tarball creation, then failed hosted-analysis because direct PM/changelog closeout commits left exact main SHA 4b13e7d1e without DeepScan status. No v2026.8.3 tag or npm artifact exists. Recovery will establish a PR-reviewed exact main head and rerun once; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-08-03T02:33:10.763Z","harness:codex","Correction to the immediately preceding August 3 recovery evidence: the evidence PR MUST be rebase-merged before rerunning hosted analysis so its reviewed head commit remains the exact main SHA carrying DeepScan status. Squash or merge-commit methods would create a different main SHA and repeat the fail-closed hosted-analysis refusal. Thresholds remain unchanged; mutable exact-head proof stays in PR #876."
  "2026-08-03T03:42:03.194Z","harness:codex","Release health verified live 2026-08-03 after the SDK provenance tranche. PR #874 merged broad SDK/CLI/MCP provenance contracts; PR #875 fixed nondeterministic procfs RSS coverage; PR #876 established immutable identical-tree hosted-analysis evidence. Auto Release run 30780200149 succeeded from main c84b37e080c7f798d00037f54e8ef120d7dedda2 and cut exactly one v2026.8.3 release commit/tag ee13855074f6c8a0609446fb5cf3df8bda2a5894. Downstream Release run 30780636912 succeeded: 6,748 tests at exact 100/100/100/100, strict static/context/docs/compat/security gates, Sentry source maps, package smoke/dogfood, npm publish, npx/bunx verification, installed npm/Bun agent-session acceptance, and GitHub release metadata. Public uncached registry metadata reports latest=2026.8.3, SLSA provenance, and integrity sha512-Eh/oYOiWfrxdXGqu9AJqebLCyglrVKwp3yXKXOuANIUh2w48ycvwlUEx+leQPX8YjfyOYxX+LsRvkmeyrzSmvw==. Independent temp-root proof downloaded that exact tarball, installed 63 npm and 61 Bun packages offline from isolated project roots, then npx --no-install pm completed version/init/create/list-open and bunx --bun pm completed version/contracts. The initial direct npx registry probe saw stale metadata and the fresh-cache retry timed out; uncached registry HTTP and the immutable tarball resolved afterward, so that was local registry transport/cache behavior rather than a missing publication. Observability: the 14-day best-effort reliability gate passed with Sentry critical=0, high=0, total=0, two expected handled issues, telemetry finish_error_rate_pct=0.71, and no missing error-code rows. Real-time delivery is NOT healthy: pm telemetry flush at 03:40:44Z drained 0 of 1,333 queued events, failed with fetch failed, and last successful flush remains 02:02:37Z. This is retained as an honest boundary and does not weaken pm-ei6x66. The recurring reminder returns to open."
  "2026-08-03T11:17:37.564Z","harness:codex","Release-health evidence 2026-08-03: npm latest is 2026.8.3; GitHub has exactly one release for the UTC day, v2026.8.3 published at 03:11:27Z; the scheduled Auto Release run 30788639874 completed successfully at 05:58Z after the earlier explicit workflow_dispatch release. Exact published-artifact verification passed registry integrity, direct and package-selected npx, direct and package-selected bunx, pm-mcp initialization under both executors, all three bin mappings, four missing-command negative controls, and non-draft non-prerelease GitHub Release metadata."
  "2026-08-03T11:27:41.256Z","harness:codex","Observability boundary 2026-08-03T11:24Z: pm health --check-only --check-telemetry reports 11 queued records, queue_draining=false, last successful flush 11:23:27Z, and last failed flush 11:24:09Z with fetch failed. The configured endpoint health probe still returns HTTP 200. This is not evidence that collector delivery is healthy: published-artifact and release checks passed independently, while real-time telemetry transport remains an explicit unresolved operational boundary. No duplicate defect was opened because this recurring release-health reminder already carries the live delivery lineage and historical transport evidence."
  "2026-08-03T20:38:41.120Z","harness:claude-code","Release health verified live 2026-08-03, recorded because the state is unchanged rather than because it moved.\n\nExactly one cut today. The scheduled Auto Release run at 05:57Z succeeded and published; five further runs fired on the issues-closed trigger and all skipped. Four workflow_dispatch runs earlier in the day failed and one at 02:48Z succeeded, none of which produced a second published version. npm latest is 2026.8.3, the tag v2026.8.3 exists, and the GitHub release is present, not a draft and not a prerelease.\n\nThe published artifact verifier passes end to end for 2026.8.3 across npm, npx and bunx. Bin coverage is complete for pm, pm-cli and pm-mcp over both distinct entrypoints, and all four negative controls observed the expected nonzero exit, so the checks can still fail.\n\nThe one-cut-per-day invariant therefore held again today under a mixed trigger load of schedule, dispatch and issues events, which is the combination most likely to breach it.\n"
  "2026-08-04T09:19:16.056Z","harness:codex","Release-health evidence 2026-08-04: npm latest and the sole GitHub release for the UTC day are 2026.8.4; scheduled Auto Release run 30880997668 and tag-driven Release run 30881541650 both succeeded. The full published-release verifier passed. Direct and package-selected npx both execute 2026.8.4, direct and package-selected bunx --bun both execute 2026.8.4 under Bun 1.3.11. Exactly one production tag exists for 2026-08-04."
  "2026-08-07T05:48:03.999Z","harness:claude-code","Release health 2026-08-07: the scheduled cut FAILED, and this is the first failure of the daily cadence since it was unblocked on 2026-07-15.\n\nWhat happened. The 04:36Z scheduled run built the candidate artifact for 2026.8.7 and then failed the Sentry reliability gate on a single high unresolved issue, PM-CLI-2W, whose title is a TypeError from the unknown-author acknowledgment surface. The product behaviour behind that error was correct: it refuses a stale or non-actionable target. The refusal simply carried no exit code, so the observability boundary reported it as a generic handled failure and the gate read it as a blocking production defect. Zero critical, one high, threshold zero.\n\nThe failure was clean. It stopped before tagging and before publishing, so no partial release exists: the remote tag set ends at v2026.8.6 and npm latest is 2026.8.6. No second cut was attempted. The one-release-per-day fence was never exercised because no cut completed.\n\nCadence context. The eight preceding runs since 2026-08-05 all fired on issue closure and all skipped, which is the healthy post-cut pattern. The 2026-08-06 05:33Z scheduled run succeeded and cut 2026.8.6.\n\nDisposition. The product fix landed in this session and was verified live on the exact invocation that produced the blocking issue, which now exits 2 with a stable code and never reaches the error channel. The gate also declares the four acknowledgment refusal families as expected-handled. Because the gate reads a rolling fourteen-day window over unresolved issues, the fix alone does not unblock the cut: the existing occurrence must be dispositioned in the external store. That manual step is the subject of a filed defect, since nothing joins a closed tracker item to the external record whose lifetime gates the release.\n"
  "2026-08-07T06:28:48.625Z","harness:claude-code","Second attempt 2026-08-07, dispatched with push enabled: the Sentry blocker is gone and the cut now fails on a different, structural gate.\n\nProgress confirmed. The reliability gate that stopped the 04:36Z scheduled run reported zero critical and zero high with no blocking issues, so the product fix plus the disposition cleared that class. The pipeline then ran the full suite, passed the exact coverage gate at 100 percent with zero uncovered counts, and built the candidate artifact for the next version.\n\nNew failure. The hosted analysis gate refused the candidate because no DeepScan status exists for the exact commit. Both analyzers run on pull-request branches only: a pull-request head on this repository carries DeepScan as a commit status and CodeFactor as a check run, while the squash commit that lands on the default branch carries neither, and the gate normally recovers through an identical-tree merge parent or the matching pull-request head. Today's candidate reached the default branch by direct push, so it has no second parent and no associated pull request, and neither recovery path applies.\n\nThis is not a transient condition. The candidate is always the current head, so every subsequent scheduled cut fails the same way until a pull-request-merged commit lands. Twenty-four repository-owned checks pass on the head, including all four coverage shards; the only thing missing is external evidence that this repository's workflow never produces for a direct push.\n\nState after the attempt: no tag was created, nothing was published, the remote tag set still ends at v2026.8.6 and npm latest is still 2026.8.6. Clean stop again, and the one-cut-per-day fence remains unexercised because no cut has completed today. Filed as its own defect.\n"
  "2026-08-07T11:23:43.930Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health check 2026-08-07. npm dist-tag latest is 2026.8.7 and the GitHub release v2026.8.7 exists. Executor verification re-run from a clean directory: `npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.7 --version`, `npx -y --package=@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.7 pm --version` and `bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.7 --version` all print 2026.8.7. Same-day idempotency exercised for real today rather than reasoned about: the scheduled run failed on a production-error gate, two recovery dispatches followed, and the second skipped on the release_already_cut_today guard while the first cut the tag — one release for the UTC day across three pipeline runs."
  "2026-08-07T17:13:56.914Z","harness:claude-code","Evening re-verification 2026-08-07, after the morning pass already recorded the three-run picture for this UTC day. State unchanged and still exactly one release for the day: npm dist-tag latest 2026.8.7, tag v2026.8.7 present and unique, package.json 2026.8.7, and the [Unreleased] changelog section empty. The 04:36Z scheduled run failed on sentry-telemetry-gate, the 10:12Z dispatch cut the tag, the 10:24Z dispatch skipped on release_already_cut_today.\n\nOne addition the morning entry does not carry: the trigger asymmetry that makes the scheduled path the least-verified one. On workflow_dispatch, push defaults to false and dry_run to false; on schedule, INPUT_PUSH is hardcoded true. A dispatch run at the default therefore exercises every gate but not the commit-tag-push path, and a dispatch run with push=true exercises a path whose same-day guard then blocks it. Neither dispatch shape reproduces the scheduled shape exactly, and the scheduled shape is the only one the daily guarantee depends on. The two most recent scheduled failures were both repaired and then released by dispatch, so no scheduled run has completed successfully at HEAD since the repairs landed. Rate evidence recorded on pm-e70zh5; the same-day guard's trigger-blindness remains on pm-uenmu9."
  "2026-08-08T14:06:54.631Z","harness:codex","2026-08-08 release-health proof: PRs #935 and #938 shipped as the sole v2026.8.8 cut. Auto Release 31259981172 and downstream Release 31260405095 succeeded; npm latest=2026.8.8 and independent npm/npx/bunx/pm-mcp/GitHub verification passed. The initial issue-recovery run 31258567364 failed on a date-specific packaged test assertion and is tracked/fixed by pm-7ipajv. Closing GH #934 triggered guarded run 31261020199, which completed in 50s using the recorded retry/same-day guard and did not create another tag. Live Sentry critical/high=0/0; telemetry error rate=0.99%, missing error-code rows=0; local flush drained cleanly."
  "2026-08-08T22:04:38.418Z","harness:claude-code","Release health 2026-08-08: 2026.8.8 is live on npm as latest and on GitHub Releases, and the published artifact runs under both npx and bunx at that version. The scheduled run at 03:52Z failed the reliability gate on two unresolved high issues (PM-CLI-2S host-capacity ENOSPC, owned by pm-3lhth4; PM-CLI-2Q a correct usage refusal whose event predates the contract-tag producer, now filed as pm-h75tjh). Both were resolved by hand and the cut happened through a manual dispatch at 13:37Z. One release for the day; the same-day guard compares parsed date components rather than a prefix glob, and a tracker-only change set skips the pipeline instead of cutting."
  "2026-08-09T02:03:23.996Z","harness:codex","2026-08-09 release attempt evidence: PR #944 merged as 26370b95a. Auto Release workflow_dispatch run 31289144441 used push=true with telemetry_mode=required and failed closed before tag or publication after passing exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, secrets, packed npx smoke, 88-command temporary dogfood, and candidate packaging. Exact failure: telemetry_query_command_missing because GitHub-hosted release runners intentionally have no private PM_TELEMETRY_QUERY_COMMAND adapter, the already documented pm-ei6x66 boundary. Remote v2026.8.9 tag, GitHub release, and npm 2026.8.9 are absent; npm remains 2026.8.8. Recovery will use the production workflow's telemetry_mode=off contract, while Sentry remains mandatory via the configured SENTRY_PERSONAL_ADMIN_TOKEN and live telemetry delivery is verified separately from an owner-local adapter."
  "2026-08-09T02:30:19.681Z","harness:codex","2026-08-09 release-health closeout: production-contract Auto Release run 31289529224 succeeded and waited for downstream Release run 31289931100. Exactly one v2026.8.9 tag exists; GitHub release is non-draft/non-prerelease; npm latest 2026.8.9 carries SLSA provenance. Independent verify-published-release passed npm integrity, direct and package-selected npx and bunx dispatch, pm-mcp initialization under both executors, all pm/pm-cli/pm-mcp bin mappings, and four missing-bin negative controls. Live Sentry 14-day reliability gate passed at critical=0/high=0 and the Sentry release pm-cli@2026.8.9 is finalized against release commit c44920a62 with zero new groups. Owner-local telemetry health returned status ok with HTTP 200 probe; an inline flush drained 3/3 queued redacted events to zero at 02:29:53Z. The recurring reminder remains open and unclaimed by design."
  "2026-08-09T07:46:34.513Z","harness:codex","2026-08-09 follow-up: scheduled Auto Release run 31293670520 completed successfully as a no-publish decision with reason tracker_only_changes_since_last_tag and explicitly reported no new pushed release tag. Public state remains exactly one v2026.8.9 tag/release for the UTC day; GitHub marks it latest, non-draft, non-prerelease, and npm latest remains 2026.8.9. The second successful Auto Release workflow status is therefore a guarded skip, not a second cut."
  "2026-08-09T16:21:35.283Z","harness:codex","2026-08-09 post-PR #952 release-health proof: main merged at 9992030e6 after the sole daily v2026.8.9 cut. A canonical release-pipeline dry run returned skipped:true with reason release_already_cut_today and exactly tags_today=[v2026.8.9], proving no ordinal or second auto-release was created. GitHub Release v2026.8.9 remains latest/non-draft/non-prerelease, npm latest remains 2026.8.9, the tag-push Release run is successful, and verify-published-release passed npm integrity plus direct/package-selected npx and bunx and pm-mcp controls. Live 14-day Sentry gate passed critical=0/high=0; unresolved visible groups are stale July handled events. Local telemetry recorded current commands with zero invalid rows and a current successful flush timestamp, but 25-27 retry-aged queued events remain advisory and an explicit flush made no bulk progress. The reminder remains open and unclaimed by design."
  "2026-08-10T00:19:43.526Z","harness:codex","Pre-merge observability evidence 2026-08-10: Sentry access is healthy but the strict 14-day reliability gate fails closed at critical=0/high=1 on PM-CLI-2X, now cross-referenced to canonical host-fault item pm-3lhth4. Local telemetry storage is valid with zero invalid rows and a recent successful-flush timestamp, but the subsequent explicit flush failed at transport and left a small retry queue; therefore real-time delivery is not claimed healthy. This recurring reminder remains open and unclaimed, and no credentials, endpoints, raw events, or hosted identifiers beyond the public Sentry short ID are recorded."
  "2026-08-10T12:24:04.856Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health verification 2026-08-10. Exactly one release exists for the day across all three ledgers, which is the property this reminder exists to confirm: npm carries 2026.8.10 and nothing else prefixed 2026.8.10, git carries the single tag v2026.8.10, and GitHub carries the single release v2026.8.10 with npm dist-tag latest pointing at it. Both published execution paths were driven against the registry artifact rather than a local build: npx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.10 --version and bunx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.10 --version each report 2026.8.10.\nThe single-cut guarantee held under load, which is the part worth recording. Six Auto Release runs fired today: the scheduled 04:15 run, a workflow_dispatch, and four issues-triggered runs from the blocker-closure path. Only one version was cut. The most recent retry declined to publish with skip reason retry_already_attempted because the blocker issue already recorded a same-day retry, and it left the blocker closed because the retry path did not fail.\nThe scheduled run itself failed, and reading the last successful run instead of the last scheduled one would have hidden it. It failed on sentry-telemetry-gate with blocking_short_ids naming an ENOTDIR fault, which is the guard-reachability defect fixed and shipped the same day: absence-tolerant readers accepted only ENOENT, so a tracker root that is a regular file raised an unclassified fault. That Sentry issue is now resolved and the four remaining unresolved issues in the project last occurred 2026-07-13 and 2026-07-14, outside the gate's recent-activity window, so the gate is currently clear rather than merely quiet.\nResidual, already owned and not re-filed: pm-db8onn for blocker closure rerunning the stale tag-push workflow, pm-e70zh5 for the unmeasured scheduled-failure rate, pm-44u3wt for scheduled runs firing hours outside their declared cron window, and pm-uenmu9 for the open disposition on whether a manually triggered same-day release should be permitted at all."
  "2026-08-13T14:39:33.237Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health verification 2026-08-13, live against the real systems rather than from the tracker.\n\nCadence: exactly one release per UTC day for eight consecutive days. gh release list shows v2026.8.6 through v2026.8.13 with one tag each; git tag agrees; npm view @unbrained/pm-cli versions ends 2026.8.8, 2026.8.9, 2026.8.10, 2026.8.11, 2026.8.12, 2026.8.13. No day carries two auto-releases. Today's cut came from the scheduled run 31667050959, which succeeded at 04:27 UTC; a manual dispatch at 03:55 the same day also succeeded and did not produce a second release, so the same-day guard held across trigger types on a day where both fired.\n\nDistribution verified by execution, not by inspection. npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.13 --version returns 2026.8.13 from a clean cache, and bunx --bun @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.13 --version returns 2026.8.13. Both resolve the published tarball rather than a local checkout.\n\nThe pipeline's own coverage matches: release.yml runs verify-published-release.mjs across npm, npx and bunx, then verify-installed-agent-session.mjs with --manager both, so npm and Bun are each driven through a scripted agent session against the exact published artifact before the GitHub release is created.\n\nStanding caveat, unchanged and separately owned: the scheduled cron is 02:35 UTC and the run fired at 04:27, which is the drift pm-44u3wt tracks. The release still happened; the clock is the undocumented part."
  "2026-08-14T14:40:58.098Z","harness:codex","Release-health evidence 2026-08-14: exactly one immutable v2026.8.14 GitHub release is present and npm latest is 2026.8.14. The scheduled Auto Release run 31769746801 completed successfully after the earlier explicitly dispatched publication; it did not create a second daily tag. pnpm release:verify-published -- --version 2026.8.14 --json passed npm metadata/integrity, npx and bunx pm/default/MCP entrypoints, all negative controls, complete bin coverage, and the non-draft non-prerelease GitHub release."
  "2026-08-16T10:43:42.983Z","harness:claude-code","Release-health check 2026-08-16: last scheduled Auto Release run 31924312921 concluded success at 03:28Z and published v2026.8.16 (GitHub release 03:54Z). npm view @unbrained/pm-cli version = 2026.8.16 with dist-tags.latest = 2026.8.16. Cross-runtime execution of the published artifact verified: npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.16 --version and bunx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.16 --version both print 2026.8.16. A bun install of the same version resolves every published entrypoint: ./sdk and the bare root each expose 1312 runtime exports, ./cli exposes runPmCli and _testOnly, and ./sdk/public-surface.json is readable from node_modules. That last check is what surfaced pm-suhxny."
  "2026-08-22T07:19:15.349Z","harness:codex","Release-health evidence 2026-08-22: workflow-dispatch Auto Release run 32545649142 published v2026.8.22; tag-driven Release run 32546288241 succeeded at exact tag SHA d7b6f18ce912ccf84d754cf5e539b4090c62c98b. The later scheduled Auto Release run 32548773304 detected the immutable same-day automatic target, skipped analyzer/build/publish steps, and completed successfully, so there was one published v2026.8.22 despite both a manual trigger and the schedule. GitHub release count for the exact tag is one, npm latest is 2026.8.22, and fresh npx plus bunx both report 2026.8.22. GitHub isImmutable remains false and stays owned by pm-k9m6wc; this is current release-path success, not proof of the thirty-day reliability SLO."
  "2026-08-23T15:19:13.928Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: reused the standing release-health lineage after all-status search found this canonical reminder. Evidence: Release run 32647119087 passed every source, test, coverage, static, assurance, compatibility, reliability, packaging, and dogfood gate, then npm 11.17.0 signed provenance but returned E404 while the publish step exported the stale NPM_TOKEN as NODE_AUTH_TOKEN. Implementing a reviewed workflow correction so publish runs with OIDC and no long-lived token."
  "2026-08-23T15:27:41.081Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: release.yml no longer exposes secrets.NPM_TOKEN to source selection or publication. Exact-version probes and npm publish both use explicit empty npmrc/cache contexts with NODE_AUTH_TOKEN and NPM_TOKEN unset, leaving GitHub OIDC as the publish credential. Updated release documentation and fail-closed workflow contracts. Verification passed: focused 37/37, build, typecheck, lint with zero clones, repository static-quality assurance, docs links, graph composition, and record integrity."
  "2026-08-23T15:37:21.147Z","harness:codex","Review feedback: Sourcery correctly identified that trusted-publisher OIDC cannot authorize npm access set. Removed the now-impossible access-recovery branch; non-public package metadata now fails closed with an explicit manual visibility-recovery instruction. Documented the one-time public-package prerequisite and extended executable contracts. Focused workflow suite remains 37/37; build and typecheck pass."
  "2026-08-23T15:40:07.156Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review evidence: removed every remaining valid NPM_TOKEN requirement and authenticated-probe/access-recovery description from the release guide, renamed the workflow diagnostic to anonymous exact-version probe, and added the diagnostic to the workflow contract. Focused contracts 37/37 and docs links pass."
  "2026-08-23T16:13:02.507Z","harness:codex","Release recovery evidence: run 32650106770 passed every source, coverage, static, assurance, Sentry, package, tarball, and dogfood gate, then npm returned ENEEDAUTH. Live log showed actions/setup-node exported uppercase NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG while the publish wrapper set lowercase npm_config_userconfig; the setup-node token-placeholder npmrc therefore retained precedence and suppressed OIDC. Implementing a fail-closed config-isolation correction with contract coverage."
  "2026-08-23T16:14:37.488Z","harness:codex","Fix evidence: removed actions/setup-node registry-url so it cannot create the token-placeholder npmrc; release probes and publish now override uppercase NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG/NPM_CONFIG_CACHE while unsetting lowercase aliases. Contracts reject registry-url and lowercase userconfig regression. Verification: focused workflow contracts 37/37, pnpm build passed, pnpm typecheck passed, docs/skills links passed."
  "2026-08-23T16:53:21.776Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-23: exact-tag recovery run 32652020474 on reviewed main 757f308bd passed build, 7,848-test exact-coverage, changelog, static, assurance, compatibility, reliability, Sentry, packaging, npx tarball, and package-first dogfood, then npm 11.17.0 returned ENEEDAUTH during npm publish. Unlike run 32650106770, setup-node no longer provided registry-url and the publish process used an isolated empty NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG, so the prior placeholder-config precedence failure is excluded. Signed-in npm package settings were re-read live and exactly show GitHub org unbraind, repository pm-cli, workflow release.yml, environment release, allowed action npm publish, public package, and strict disallow-bypass-token publishing policy. Next recovery must expose the otherwise-suppressed OIDC token-exchange diagnostic before running the long release gates; item remains the permanently-open standing reminder."
  "2026-08-23T16:56:13.589Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added an early tokenless npm trusted-publisher dry-run to release.yml. It uses isolated empty npm config/cache paths, strips classic token variables, requests OIDC through npm itself at verbose log level, passes only when npm reports a successful token exchange, prints only sanitized oidc/auth diagnostic lines on refusal, and runs before the 7,848-test release gate. Contracts and docs prevent drift. Verification: focused CI/release workflow contracts 37/37 passed; pnpm build passed; pnpm typecheck passed; docs link gate passed; Prettier check passed after formatting. The standalone local actionlint binary is unavailable, so the pinned GitHub security workflow remains the syntax authority."
  "2026-08-23T19:25:53.821Z","harness:codex","Release-health completion 2026-08-23: immutable tag v2026.8.23 remains at 52a1f8f88e9e842215220eb79d8c453d5fc98a7f. Release run 32660082029 succeeded on reviewed main 5f828914ce0ce6a8eea0653f0aeb064a30cfc951, including early tokenless trusted-publisher exchange, build, 7,848-test exact coverage, changelog, static, assurance, compatibility, reliability, Sentry sourcemaps, package/tarball/dogfood gates, npm publish, npm/npx/bunx verification, npm+Bun installed-agent acceptance, GitHub release creation, and metadata verification. Public npm @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.23 reports integrity sha512-PWdl9O4ZLc3G8a74RkSCQMfJAkkuL3G9rZJHdA/0rFPsyFlSQteKX8lX/2NrN10NaKD0t7YdNCj21PJ1u6+2zQ==; independent published-release and installed-agent verifiers passed. Incident #1095 was closed with evidence; issue-triggered Auto Release run 32661134479 then succeeded via the immutable same-day retry-skip guard without a duplicate cut. Keep this standing reminder open."
  "2026-08-24T13:34:18.531Z","harness:codex","Release-health completion 2026-08-24: delivery PR #1101 merged as 576ab65e91a4020c19c846e206f4eade25b49f14; release-fixture recovery PR #1106 merged as 71d6ad99e9efa23548815855a7bf0386acf82b7e after exact-head Bugbot and Security reviews were clean. Exact merged-main CI, Security, CodeQL, Docs, OSSF, and CodSpeed workflows passed. Production Auto Release run 32729950508 cut immutable tag v2026.8.24 at release commit 1c1fcf8dea5cb9789c6164c4c1c9691f20f0fff6, whose sole parent is reviewed main 71d6ad99e9efa23548815855a7bf0386acf82b7e; exact-tag Release run 32731192102 passed. GitHub Release is public; npm latest is 2026.8.24 with integrity sha512-X95ly1p9hhJSuDzDC4yj1f+ctM2rWn+zn01JxaLsw3KBIXBr1hIyPk2YcpAvS0OLIvD2XkFHOV8j19xlmjcvXA== and unpacked size 19021048. Fresh npx and bunx returned 2026.8.24; independent published-release verification passed; fresh installed npm and Bun agent sessions each passed all 11 lifecycle steps. GitHub blocker #1102 is closed. Post-release Sentry/telemetry threshold passed at critical=0 and high=0 over 14 days. Telemetry flush delivered 1 queued event with queue_progressed=true and queue_empty=true. Standing reminder remains open and is re-armed for 2026-08-25 06:00 UTC."
  "2026-08-25T08:01:23.350Z","harness:codex","Release-health evidence 2026-08-25: PR #1113 merged after today's scheduled release as main 74632a9ceb246cabcdb37f52b943af2dd45c7a84. Exact-main CI, release-analyzer provenance, Windows, coverage, static, CodeQL, Security, Docs, OSSF, and CodSpeed all passed. The already-published v2026.8.25 tag points to fb094d038aac2f51f3f3ebbc16c178d9c43d979a and therefore does not contain PR #1113; same-day duplicate publication remains forbidden, so this delivery is queued for the 2026-08-26 daily cut. Today's public artifact is healthy: independent verifier passed npm, npx, bunx, MCP handshakes, bin coverage, negative controls, and GitHub Release; Sentry critical=0 high=0 and telemetry finish_error_rate_pct=2.52 with zero missing error-code rows."
  "2026-08-25T10:43:54.984Z","harness:codex","Release-health handoff 2026-08-25: PR #1115 merged to main as e2db01f8064edd54fc2edd38c8c045678c39b439 after exact-main CI run 32837789784 passed. The existing v2026.8.25 tag, GitHub Release, and npm latest were created before this merge, so they do not contain PR #1115. Public 2026.8.25 distribution health was independently verified through isolated npm, npx, bunx, MCP, and cold installed npm/Bun consumer workflows. The 14-day Sentry/telemetry gate reports critical=0 and high=0, and the bounded live Sentry unresolved inventory is empty. Reminder is re-armed for 2026-08-26 to prove the first eligible daily release contains e2db01f8 or a descendant and to re-check all distribution, analyzer, observability, and physical queue requirements."
  "2026-08-29T10:03:37.112Z","harness:codex","2026-08-29 release-health incident: scheduled Auto Release run 33245252202 failed at the pre-build hosted analyzer gate for direct-main docs commit e88b8ae74fd7a5a52ee6fbb21025f45c2cf3cf5b. This is the intended fail-closed policy from pm-u1baah, not a publish attempt: no gate artifact, tag, npm version, or GitHub Release was created. PR #1149 includes a reviewed descendant and will supply analyzer provenance; after merge, dispatch/observe one release attempt and verify tag, GitHub Release, npm, npx, bunx, Sentry, and telemetry before releasing this standing reminder."
  "2026-08-29T10:18:56.874Z","harness:codex","Auto-release recovery evidence update: the consolidated delivery now passes exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, repository static assurance, secret scanning, package boundary/parity, graph and record-integrity gates, and pm-changelog 2026.8.29 validation. Issue #1153 documents the fail-closed scheduled run on unreviewed direct-main docs commit e88b8ae74fd7a5a52ee6fbb21025f45c2cf3cf5b; no tag or package was published. After PR #1149 merges with exact-head analyzer provenance, dispatch one reviewed-main recovery run only after confirming no same-day AUTO release exists."
  "2026-08-29T19:52:12.404Z","harness:codex","Live failure evidence 2026-08-29: workflow_dispatch Auto Release run 33271219991 on reviewed main 9baed9829 failed before creating any tag, GitHub Release, or npm artifact. The mandatory npx-smoke gate passed npx then failed spawnSync bunx ENOENT because auto-release.yml, unlike the already-fixed CI and Release workflows, did not provision Bun. Public state remains npm 2026.8.28 with no v2026.8.29. Recovery must add pinned Bun setup to the auto-release gate runner, prove ordering by TDD, merge through review, and only then rerun the unpublished target."
  "2026-08-29T19:59:15.109Z","harness:codex","Recovery implementation evidence: TDD added the auto-release Bun provision/order contract first; the focused workflow suite failed 1/14 because setup-bun was absent. The workflow now installs Bun via the same SHA-pinned setup-bun v2 action, under the same no-existing-tag guard as pnpm/Node, before the auto-release pipeline can invoke the mandatory npx+bunx packed smoke. Focused tests pass 14/14 and the complete pnpm lint suite passes with zero ESLint warnings, zero jscpd clones, and all static, SDK, token, graph, and record-integrity gates green."
  "2026-08-29T20:18:35.436Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence: Sourcery identified that the Auto Release workflow contract did not prove Setup Bun shared the immutable-target guard; Greptile identified that bun-version: latest made release tooling non-reproducible. TDD reproduced both contract gaps. The workflow contract now requires the exact immutable-target guard, the pinned setup-bun action, and Bun 1.4.0. CI, Auto Release, and Release all use the same pinned Bun 1.4.0 toolchain. Focused workflow-contract verification passed 14/14; full pnpm lint passed ESLint with zero warnings, zero jscpd clones, repository-static-quality, SDK/package/grammar/flag/refusal/token, graph-composition, tracker-context-quality, and record-integrity gates."
notes[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-02T06:41:55.766Z",claude-code-agent,"2026-07-02: Auto Release run 28569991109 success; tag v2026.7.2 created and npm dist-tags.latest=2026.7.2 verified live via npm view. Release-commit CI/Release/CodeQL/Docs all green. Release health verified."
  "2026-07-04T06:16:41.031Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-04: Release v2026.7.4 verified — Release workflow 28697208639 succeeded, npm @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.4 live, GH release published 06:16Z (not draft). Auto-release healthy."
  "2026-07-04T06:52:55.930Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-04 verified: v2026.7.4 tagged and npm latest advanced (published 06:15:46Z). Auto-release healthy."
  "2026-07-04T08:13:20.569Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-04 release-health verified: Auto Release run 28697011506 success, tag v2026.7.4 Release workflow success (8m58s), npm latest = 2026.7.4."
  "2026-07-04T10:39:22.817Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-04 release-health check: npm view @unbrained/pm-cli version → 2026.7.4 (matches today's date-based cut); Auto Release scheduled run 28697011506 succeeded (17m9s), post-release CI/CodeQL/Docs/Security workflows on the release commit all green. Only red run today is Nightly Validation windows-latest/Node 24 (GH-427, fix in working tree via pm-lt6n)."
  "2026-07-04T19:01:16.920Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-04 release-health verified live: git tag v2026.7.4 exists and npm view @unbrained/pm-cli version = 2026.7.4 (latest advanced). Today's merges to main (PR #428 head + close-message fallback d3e37991) will ride the next daily cut once [Unreleased] is non-empty."
  "2026-07-06T07:51:41.740Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-06 audit #7 verification: npm latest = 2026.7.6 (published 2026-07-06T07:10Z); scheduled Auto Release run 28773444589 succeeded in 18m41s. Yesterday's scheduled run 28731921751 failed after 1m07s but the blocker-resolution retry path (PR #451) + manual dispatch 28746204455 published 2026.7.5 same day. Release pipeline healthy."
  "2026-07-30T09:21:47.402Z","harness:claude-code","Release procedure verified live 2026-07-30. Exactly one auto-release cut today: push-triggered run 30516964641 at 05:33Z, conclusion success. npm dist-tag latest = 2026.7.30; published versions end 2026.7.26, 2026.7.27, 2026.7.28, 2026.7.29, 2026.7.30 - one artifact per day, no same-day double. Git tag v2026.7.30 present.\n\nPublished-artifact acceptance, both package managers, against the real registry copy rather than a local build: npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.30 runs --version, init, create and list end to end; bunx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.7.30 does the same under bun 1.3.11. Both created a real item and listed it back."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T13:11:41.088Z","harness:codex","Credential fallback must follow the gate's access obligation, not only its strictness mode: a configured but stale environment token is stronger evidence that Sentry access is expected, so best-effort should try the authenticated CLI before failing the release while tokenless best-effort may remain optional."
  "2026-07-26T15:52:22.655Z","harness:codex","A hidden npm package version can return 404 to both anonymous and authenticated metadata reads while the immutable publish endpoint still knows the version exists. Same-tag recovery must use the access mutation as the existence-sensitive operation, permit publish only on a definitive package-not-found response, and fail closed for every credential or registry error."
